gonometric Identities of Sum and Difference of Angles","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"$\\cos^2 A - \\sin^2 A$ equals:","options":{"A":"$\\cos 2A$","B":"$\\sin 2A$","C":"$1 - 2\\sin^2 A$","D":"Both (a) and (c)"}},{"chapter":"Trigonometric Identities of Sum and Difference of Angles","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"If $\\tan A = \\frac{1}{2}$, then $\\tan 2A$ equals:","options":{"A":"$\\frac{4}{3}$","B":"$\\frac{3}{4}$","C":"$1$","D":"$\\frac{2}{3}$"}},{"chapter":"Trigonometric Identities of Sum and Difference of Angles","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"$2 \\sin 45^\\circ \\cos 45^\\circ$ equals:","options":{"A":"$1$","B":"$0$","C":"$\\frac{1}{2}$","D":"$\\sqrt{2}$"}},{"chapter":"Application of Trigonometry","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"In any triangle $ABC$, with usual notation, the area of the triangle is:","options":{"A":"$\\frac{1}{2}ab \\sin C$","B":"$\\frac{1}{2}bc \\sin A$","C":"$\\frac{1}{2}ca \\sin B$","D":"(All of these)"}},{"chapter":"Application of Trigonometry","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"In any triangle $ABC$, $a \\cos B + b \\cos A$ equals:","options":{"A":"$c$","B":"$b$","C":"$a$","D":"$0$"}},{"chapter":"Application of Trigonometry","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"The law of sines states that in any triangle $ABC$:","options":{"A":"$\\frac{a}{\\sin A} = \\frac{b}{\\sin B} = \\frac{c}{\\sin C}$","B":"$\\frac{a}{\\cos A} = \\frac{b}{\\cos B} = \\frac{c}{\\cos C}$","C":"$a^2 = b^2 + c^2 - 2bc\\cos A$","D":"$a = b = c$"}},{"chapter":"Application of Trigonometry","section":"A","type":"mcq","source":"important_book","year":null,"text":"The cosine rule for side $a$ in triangle $ABC$ is:","options":{"A":"$a^2 = b^2 + c^2 - 2bc \\cos A$","B":"$a^2 = b^2 + c^2 + 2bc \\cos A$","C":"$a^2 = b^2 - c^2 + 2bc \\cos A$","